node.doctext:
Another potential danger of [doc://glob] is its usage in scalar context. It should return the matches one by one,  but the iterator is assigned to the place where [doc://glob] is used and isn't reset when a new parameter is supplied to it:
<c>
#! /usr/bin/perl
use warnings;
use strict;
use feature qw{ say };

open my $fh, '>', $_ for my @files = qw( a1 a2 b1 b2 );

for my $mask ('a*', 'b*') {
    while (my $f = glob $mask) {
        say $f;
        last
    }
}

unlink @files;
</c><P>

<spoiler>Yes, this returns no strings starting with b.</spoiler><P>


